    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0564" n="554" xml:id="pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minutes of Meeting Between General Marshall and General
                        Pee</hi><anchor n="40" xml:id="d287-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">at No. 5 Ning Hai Road, Nanking, November 19, 1946, 5:30
                        p.m.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Nanking</placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1946-11-19T17:30:00+08:00">November 19, 1946, 5:30 p.m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>General Pee told General Marshall that the Generalissimo instructed him to report
                    that Mister Carsun Chang, representing the major part of the Democratic
                    Socialists, will probably come into the National Assembly tomorrow. The
                    procedure will be settled sometime this evening. Apart from the Communists,
                    about three-fourths or two-thirds of the opposition parties have now joined in
                    the Assembly. Tomorrow the names of delegates will be announced to
                    participate.</p>
                <p>General Marshall thanked General Pee for this information and inquired what
                    business was transacted by the National Assembly today.</p>
                <p>General Pee stated that he did not know, but that the Generalissimo attended the
                    Assembly this morning.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
